<p class="lt-chem-371697">If we know the mass, <em>m</em>, of a sample and its specific heat capacity, <em>c</em>, we can calculate the heat transferred to or from the sample by measuring the temperature change during heating or cooling:</p>

<p class="mt-align-center lt-chem-371697"><em>q = </em><em>m&middot;c&middot;</em>&Delta;<em>T</em><em> = m&middot;c&middot;(</em><em>T</em><sub>final</sub><em>&ndash; </em><em>T</em><sub>initial</sub><em>)</em></p>

<p class="lt-chem-371697">The sign of &Delta;<em>T</em> tells us whether the substance is being heated (positive value for <em>q</em>) or cooled (negative <em>q</em> ).</p>

