<p class="lt-chem-371697">Chlorine monofluoride can react with fluorine to form chlorine trifluoride:</p>

<p class="lt-chem-371697">\[(i)\;\text{ClF}(g) + \text{F}_2(g) \longrightarrow \text{ClF}_3(g) \;\;\;\;\; \Delta _\text{r}H\text{&deg;}= \;? \nonumber \]</p>

<p class="lt-chem-371697">Use the reactions here to determine the &Delta;<em><sub>r</sub>H</em><em>&deg;</em> for reaction <em>(i)</em>:</p>

<p class="lt-chem-371697">\[(ii)\;2\text{OF}_2(g) \longrightarrow \text{O}_2(g) + 2\text{F}_2(g) \;\;\;\;\; \Delta _\text{r}H\text{&deg;}_{(ii)} = -49.4 \;\text{kJ/mol} \nonumber \]</p>

<p class="lt-chem-371697">\[(iii)\;2\text{ClF}(g) + \text{O}_2(g) \longrightarrow \text{Cl}_2 \text{O}(g) + \text{OF}_2(g) \;\;\;\;\; \Delta _\text{r}H\text{&deg;}_{(iii)} = +205.6 \;\text{kJ/mol} \nonumber \]</p>

<p class="lt-chem-371697">\[(iv)\;\text{ClF}_3(g) + \text{O}_2(g) \longrightarrow \dfrac{1}{2}\text{Cl}_2 \text{O}(g) + \dfrac{3}{2} \text{OF}_2(g) \;\;\;\;\; \Delta_\text{r}H\text{&deg;}_{(iv)} = +266.7 \;\text{kJ/mol} \nonumber \]</p>

